SPAdes 4.2.0 -> Emscripten: C/C++ platform guards (no behaviour change on native platforms).

* llvm-support SwapByteOrder.h: emscripten (musl) provides <endian.h> like Linux.
* llvm-support Path.inc: getMainExecutable() has no implementation for emscripten
  (#error); SPAdes never calls it, so return "".
* cppformat format.cc: _GNU_SOURCE is predefined by emscripten's clang in C++ mode, but
  musl only has the XSI (int-returning) strerror_r.
* easel esl_cpu.c: cpuid inline asm does not exist on wasm; report SSE/SSE2/SSE4.1, which
  emscripten implements on top of wasm SIMD128 (easel/hmmer are only used by the
  biosynthetic/corona HMM modes, not by --isolate).
* xxhash.h: with -msimd128 xxhash picks <arm_neon.h> (SIMDe), and emscripten's copy pulls in
  <emscripten.h>, whose C++ templates break inside xxhash's extern "C" block. Use the scalar
  XXH3 path on emscripten (hash values are identical by specification).
* xmath.h: uses ::size_t without including a header that declares it; older libc++ leaked
  it through <limits>/<cmath>, emscripten's libc++ (LLVM 24) does not.
* folly PackedSyncPtr.h: packs a pointer into the low 48 bits of a 64-bit word; valid for
  wasm64 (heap <= 16 GB). (wasm32 would need a 64-bit storage word instead of uintptr_t.)

